    "reasoning": "q-106412: The vertex is (0,0), so the parabola has equation y=ax². Using (4,-8) gives a=-1/2. Option 4 eliminates to y=-x²/2 and covers every real x; it agrees with MA's solution, differing only in spacing. q-81831: A maps (a,b) to (b,-a), rotating clockwise by π/2. The original upper-left vector becomes the steep upper-right vector in option 2. MA's worked-solution image shows that same result together with the original vector, confirming the earlier answer. q-32139: The coefficient determinant is -46, giving the inverse matrix in option 3. Multiplication produces the solution (-4,9), which satisfies both equations and confirms the earlier answer. The source uses x to denote the solution vector in this matrix expression. Each answer is supported by its own captured worked solution; no grade evidence was supplied.",
